# OpenShell console code owners. GitHub requests a review from these owners,
# and the organization's main-integrity ruleset needs one code owner's approval
# to merge. Owners are teams, so a maintainer joins or leaves in the
# organization's team settings and this file does not change.

# The console's maintainers own everything by default. The team has more than
# one member, so each can approve the other's pull requests.
* @ai-openshell/console

# CI and release automation: these hold the credentials that publish images and
# charts and push branches, so a change gets a security review from the
# organization's infra team. A later rule wins, so these override the default
# above.
/.github/ @ai-openshell/infra
/scripts/release/ @ai-openshell/infra
/scripts/retag-image.sh @ai-openshell/infra
/scripts/branch-tip.sh @ai-openshell/infra
/scripts/quay-login.sh @ai-openshell/infra
/deploy/ci/upstream/ @ai-openshell/infra
